cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or results obtained with it, please cite it as
  below. Citation is also required by the attribution terms in
  ADDITIONAL-TERMS.md for redistributed or modified versions.
type: software
title: "Uncertainty: measurement uncertainty evaluation software (GUM and Monte Carlo)"
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/unilker/uncertainty"
authors:
  # TODO: complete with full name, ORCID and affiliation before the first release.
  - family-names: "[FAMILY NAME]"
    given-names: "[GIVEN NAME]"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    # affiliation: "[AFFILIATION]"
keywords:
  - measurement uncertainty
  - GUM
  - Monte Carlo method
  - JCGM 101
  - metrology
  - analytical chemistry
  - uncertainty budget
abstract: >-
  Open software for the evaluation of measurement uncertainty according to
  the GUM uncertainty framework (JCGM 100:2008) and the Monte Carlo method of
  GUM Supplement 1 (JCGM 101:2008), with bottom-up and top-down approaches for
  analytical chemistry and calibration, a validated library of worked
  examples, and Turkish and English user guides.
